<resources>
    <!--
         nicki: declare the RGB notification/battery LED to the LineageOS platform
         (org.lineageos.platform / LightsCapabilities). The lineage-sdk default is 8
         (LIGHTS_PULSATING_LED only), so without this the framework believes there
         is no notification or battery LED and never drives it, even though the HAL
         and the fih_led kernel driver work. The previous override lived under
         overlay/vendor/cmsdk/cm/res, a dead CM-era path that targets nothing.

         1  = LIGHTS_RGB_NOTIFICATION_LED  (notification light is color adjustable)
         2  = LIGHTS_RGB_BATTERY_LED       (battery light is color adjustable)
         8  = LIGHTS_PULSATING_LED         (notification light can pulse)
         64 = LIGHTS_BATTERY_LED           (device HAS a battery light)
         total 75

         Note: bit 64 is required for the battery light to work at all, because
         LineageBatteryLights.isSupported() gates on LIGHTS_BATTERY_LED (64), not
         LIGHTS_RGB_BATTERY_LED (2). The lineage-sdk "set this to 11" comment
         predates the 64 bit.
    -->
    <integer name="config_deviceLightCapabilities">75</integer>
</resources>
